UNIT6({ unit: 14, name: "A parcel to England", icon: "📦", who: "Post office clerk", face: "👩‍💼", client: "Customer", cface: "🧑",
  turns: [
    T("Good morning. What can I do for you?", "Di que quieres enviar este paquete a Inglaterra y pregunta cuánto cuesta el envío.", "I'd like to send this parcel to England. How much does the shipping cost?|I want to send this package to England. How much is the shipping?", "parcel/package ; shipping",
      "I'd like to send this packet to England. How much does the shipping cost? :: Something we send by post is a 'parcel' (or 'package').", "I'd like to send this parcel to England. How much costs the shipping? :: Question: How much does the shipping cost?", "q"),
    T("It weighs twenty kilos, so it's forty euros. What's inside?", "Di que hay unas latas de judías y un tarro de miel.", "There are some tins of beans and a jar of honey.|Some cans of beans and a jar of honey.", "tins/cans ; beans ; jar ; honey",
      "There are some boxes of beans and a jar of honey. :: Beans come in a tin or a can.", "There are some tins of beans and a bottle of honey. :: Honey comes in a jar."),
    T("Sorry, could you speak up? You're whispering.", "Discúlpate: te da vergüenza porque el paquete está a punto de reventar.", "Sorry, I'm embarrassed. The parcel is about to burst.|Sorry, I'm a bit embarrassed. The package is about to burst.", "embarrassed ; burst",
      "Sorry, I'm embarrassing. The parcel is about to burst. :: How you feel is 'embarrassed'.", "Sorry, I'm embarrassed. The parcel is about to bursting. :: 'About to' + base verb: burst."),
    T("Don't worry. I'll wrap it with this striped tape.", "Pregunta si tiene cinta con otro dibujo, por ejemplo de lunares.", "Have you got tape with a different pattern, with spots?|Do you have tape with another pattern, with spots?", "pattern ; spots",
      "Have you got tape with a different drawing, with spots? :: A design on fabric or paper is a 'pattern'.", "Have you got tape with a different pattern, with points? :: Round dots on a pattern are 'spots'.", "q"),
  ], end: "Here you are, spots! I'm astonished it all fits.",
  staff: [
    W("Saluda y pregunta qué puedes hacer por él.", "Good morning. What can I do for you?|Hello. What can I do for you?", "what ; do for you",
      "Good morning. What can I make for you? :: The phrase is 'What can I DO for you?'.", "Good morning. What I can do for you? :: Question order: What can I do…?", "q"),
    W("Di que pesa veinte kilos, que son cuarenta euros, y pregunta qué hay dentro.", "It weighs twenty kilos, so it's forty euros. What's inside?|It's twenty kilos, so forty euros. What's inside?", "kilos ; euros ; inside",
      "It weights twenty kilos, so it's forty euros. What's inside? :: The verb is 'weigh'; 'weight' is the noun.", "It weighs twenty kilos, so it's forty euros. What's in? :: Ask 'What's inside?'.", "q"),
    W("Pide que hable más alto: está susurrando.", "Sorry, could you speak up? You're whispering.|Could you speak up, please? You're whispering.", "speak up ; whispering",
      "Sorry, could you speak up? You're whistling. :: Speaking very quietly is 'whispering'.", "Sorry, could you speak more up? You're whispering. :: The phrasal verb is 'speak up'.", "p"),
    W("Tranquilízalo: lo envolverás con esta cinta de rayas.", "Don't worry. I'll wrap it with this striped tape.|Don't worry, I'll wrap it with this striped tape.", "worry ; wrap ; striped",
      "Don't worry. I'll wrap it with this spotted tape. :: Lines are 'stripes': striped tape.", "Don't worry. I wrap it with this striped tape. :: A promise or decision now: I'll wrap."),
    W("Dale el paquete con cinta de lunares y di que te asombra que quepa todo.", "Here you are, spots! I'm astonished it all fits.|There you go. I'm astonished it all fits!", "astonished ; fits",
      "Here you are, spots! I'm astonishing it all fits. :: How you feel is 'astonished'.", "Here you are, spots! I'm astonished it all fit. :: Present simple: it all fits."),
  ], bye: "Thank you. Goodbye!" });

UNIT6({ unit: 15, name: "A remarkable necklace", icon: "💎", who: "Jeweller", face: "👨‍💼", client: "Customer", cface: "🧔",
  turns: [
    T("Welcome! Are you looking for some jewellery?", "Di que sí, buscas un collar de perlas para tu mujer.", "Yes, I'm looking for a pearl necklace for my wife.|Yes, a pearl necklace for my wife, please.", "pearl ; necklace",
      "Yes, I'm looking for a pearls necklace for my wife. :: A noun used like an adjective stays singular: a pearl necklace.", "Yes, I'm looking for a pearl collar for my wife. :: Jewellery worn round the neck is a 'necklace'."),
    T("This one is remarkable. Look at the contrast between the white pearls and the black stone.", "Di que es muy llamativo y pregunta si hay pendientes a juego.", "It's very striking. Are there any earrings to match?|It's striking. Have you got earrings to match?", "striking ; earrings",
      "It's very strike. Are there any earrings to match? :: Use the adjective: striking.", "It's very striking. Are there any rings to match? :: For your ears: earrings.", "q"),
    T("Yes, here. The pearls come from divers in Japan. They dive very deep.", "Pregunta si las perlas se pueden aplastar fácilmente.", "Can pearls be crushed easily?|Can the pearls be crushed easily?", "crushed ; easily",
      "Can pearls be crashed easily? :: Pressing something hard is 'crush'; 'crash' means to hit.", "Can pearls be crush easily? :: Passive: be crushed.", "q"),
    T("No, they're quite strong. But keep them out of the sun.", "Di que vale: el servicio ha sido excelente y las guardarás a la sombra.", "OK. The service has been excellent. I'll keep them in the shade.|Fine. Your service is excellent. I'll keep them in the shade.", "excellent ; shade",
      "OK. The service has been excellent. I'll keep them in the shadow. :: A cool place out of the sun is 'the shade'.", "OK. The service has been excellently. I'll keep them in the shade. :: Use the adjective: excellent."),
  ], end: "Thank you, sir. Your wife will look remarkable!",
  staff: [
    W("Da la bienvenida y pregunta si busca joyas.", "Welcome! Are you looking for some jewellery?|Hello! Are you looking for jewellery?", "looking ; jewellery/jewelry",
      "Welcome! Are you looking for some jewelleries? :: 'Jewellery' is uncountable: no -s.", "Welcome! Are you looking some jewellery? :: We say 'look FOR'.", "q"),
    W("Di que este es extraordinario y que mire el contraste entre las perlas blancas y la piedra negra.", "This one is remarkable. Look at the contrast between the white pearls and the black stone.|It's remarkable. Look at the contrast between the white pearls and the black stone.", "remarkable ; contrast ; pearls",
      "This one is remarkable. Look at the contrast among the white pearls and the black stone. :: For two things: between.", "This one is remarkable. Look the contrast between the white pearls and the black stone. :: We say look AT."),
    W("Di que sí, y explica que las perlas vienen de buceadores de Japón que bucean muy hondo.", "Yes, here. The pearls come from divers in Japan. They dive very deep.|The pearls come from divers in Japan. They dive very deep.", "divers ; dive ; deep",
      "Yes, here. The pearls come from drivers in Japan. They dive very deep. :: People who dive are 'divers'.", "Yes, here. The pearls come from divers in Japan. They dive very deeply down. :: Say 'dive very deep'."),
    W("Di que no, son bastante resistentes, pero que no les dé el sol.", "No, they're quite strong. But keep them out of the sun.|They're quite strong, but keep them out of the sun.", "strong ; out of the sun",
      "No, they're quite strong. But keep them out the sun. :: We say 'out OF the sun'.", "No, they're quite strongs. But keep them out of the sun. :: Adjectives have no plural: strong."),
    W("Da las gracias y di que su mujer estará guapísima.", "Thank you, sir. Your wife will look remarkable!|Thank you. Your wife will look remarkable.", "wife ; look ; remarkable",
      "Thank you, sir. Your wife will look remarkably! :: After 'look' use an adjective.", "Thank you, sir. Your wife will looks remarkable! :: After 'will', base verb: look."),
  ], bye: "Thank you. Goodbye!" });

